251
00:14:34,684 --> 00:14:37,988
- Take credit cards?
- It's cash only, sorry.

252
00:14:37,988 --> 00:14:40,623
Really? Oh.

253
00:14:40,756 --> 00:14:43,326
You only have one guard
and no cameras.

254
00:14:43,459 --> 00:14:46,029
Where I come from,
very risky.

255
00:14:46,162 --> 00:14:48,031
We don't get
much crime here.

256
00:14:48,164 --> 00:14:49,732
Oh, that's good.

257
00:14:51,001 --> 00:14:53,003
So, who owns this shithole?

258
00:14:54,004 --> 00:14:55,538
Uh, excuse me?

259
00:14:57,873 --> 00:14:59,142
I said...

260
00:14:59,275 --> 00:15:01,711
who owns this shithole?

261
00:15:02,578 --> 00:15:05,181
- Uh, Bodhi.
- Where's Bodhi?

262
00:15:05,315 --> 00:15:06,616
In his office?

263
00:15:06,749 --> 00:15:08,818
Are you asking me
or telling me?

264
00:15:11,587 --> 00:15:13,123
Go get Bodhi.

265
00:15:13,256 --> 00:15:16,026
I-- I can't leave
the desk, man.

266
00:15:19,295 --> 00:15:20,596
Hey...

267
00:15:20,730 --> 00:15:23,299
put down the pork rinds
and get Bodhi.

268
00:15:23,433 --> 00:15:26,236
- What?
- You heard me, Jumbo.

269
00:15:26,369 --> 00:15:28,471
Get Bodhi.

270
00:15:30,806 --> 00:15:33,043
Listen, asshole,
take a hike.

271
00:15:34,210 --> 00:15:36,379
Come on, man,
time to go.

272
00:15:41,484 --> 00:15:43,186
[doorbell jingling]

273
00:15:43,319 --> 00:15:45,055
You got a tire iron?

274
00:15:45,055 --> 00:15:47,057
Yeah, yeah,
I can go to the back and--

275
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:48,458
Forget it.

276
00:15:48,591 --> 00:15:50,593
- Hey, yo, that's my juice.
- Ssh.

277
00:15:51,627 --> 00:15:53,063
Anybody got the time?

278
00:15:53,196 --> 00:15:55,065
All right, listen,
mister, I told you to--

279
00:15:55,165 --> 00:15:56,866
- Aah!
- Oh, my God!

280
00:15:58,168 --> 00:15:59,969
Okay, what the fuck, Clint.

281
00:16:00,103 --> 00:16:02,538
You must be Bodhi.

282
00:16:03,673 --> 00:16:05,941
Yeah, who the--
who are you?

283
00:16:06,076 --> 00:16:08,211
- What's your name again?
- Clint.

284
00:16:08,344 --> 00:16:10,513
Clint.
Stand next to Clint.

285
00:16:11,381 --> 00:16:13,883
Is this a robbery? Fuck.

286
00:16:15,551 --> 00:16:16,919
Fred?

287
00:16:17,087 --> 00:16:18,688
Oh, my God,
is he dead?

288
00:16:18,821 --> 00:16:20,490
Nah, he's taking a break.

289
00:16:20,623 --> 00:16:22,958
Excuse me, sweetheart.

290
00:16:23,093 --> 00:16:25,595
Are you waiting
for an engraved invitation?

291
00:16:25,728 --> 00:16:28,598
I'm way too fucking high
for this, can--

292
00:16:28,731 --> 00:16:31,167
can I just wait it out
over here, please?

293
00:16:31,301 --> 00:16:33,936
Put your phone on the counter
and take a seat.

294
00:16:34,837 --> 00:16:36,972
I need to see your books.

295
00:16:37,107 --> 00:16:38,441
My books?

296
00:16:38,574 --> 00:16:40,243
Your books,
your ledgers, files,

297
00:16:40,376 --> 00:16:41,644
whatever you got.

298
00:16:41,777 --> 00:16:44,514
Are you...
from the government?

299
00:16:44,647 --> 00:16:47,016
I just knocked
your guard out, cold,

300
00:16:47,150 --> 00:16:49,152
and you think I'm a CPA?

301
00:16:49,985 --> 00:16:52,155
So, you're not
with the government.

302
00:16:52,288 --> 00:16:54,457
Let's take a walk.

303
00:16:55,825 --> 00:16:58,728
Look at these numbers.
You're making a fortune.

304
00:16:58,861 --> 00:17:00,930
[sighing, chuckling]

305
00:17:01,131 --> 00:17:03,666
So, where are you
keeping this money?

306
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,835
It's in the bank.

307
00:17:08,938 --> 00:17:10,573
I swear, it's in the bank.

308
00:17:10,706 --> 00:17:12,942
Only states
legalized this stuff.

309
00:17:13,143 --> 00:17:15,611
You put that money
in the bank,

310
00:17:15,745 --> 00:17:17,180
and the Feds will
have it by morning.

311
00:17:17,313 --> 00:17:19,449
Even you're smart enough
to know that.

312
00:17:19,582 --> 00:17:21,684
I'm not lying to you.

313
00:17:21,817 --> 00:17:23,953
Let me paint you a picture.

314
00:17:24,154 --> 00:17:26,156
You see my shoe?

315
00:17:26,289 --> 00:17:27,423
Yeah.

316
00:17:27,557 --> 00:17:29,058
Now, I'm gonna take the heel

317
00:17:29,192 --> 00:17:31,394
of my right shoe,
which is very sharp,

318
00:17:31,527 --> 00:17:32,795
and stomp it--

319
00:17:32,928 --> 00:17:35,064
[thud]
- very hard

320
00:17:35,198 --> 00:17:37,167
on the top
of your left foot,

321
00:17:37,267 --> 00:17:40,069
breaking at least
three or four metatarsals.

322
00:17:41,371 --> 00:17:43,906
It's excruciating.
I don't wanna do it.

323
00:17:44,039 --> 00:17:46,676
So, let me ask you again.

324
00:17:47,643 --> 00:17:51,013
Could it be in the desk?
Could it be in the microwave?

325
00:17:51,181 --> 00:17:55,518
Or could the safe be
behind that...

326
00:17:55,651 --> 00:17:57,720
silly poster?

327
00:18:05,961 --> 00:18:08,063
You don't need
to put yourself through this.

328
00:18:08,198 --> 00:18:11,367
I wanna be your friend,
I want you to be my friend.

329
00:18:11,501 --> 00:18:13,068
I don't wanna hurt your feet.

330
00:18:13,203 --> 00:18:16,372
Just open
the safe, please.

331
00:18:18,874 --> 00:18:20,443
My God.

332
00:18:20,576 --> 00:18:22,212
How much you got there?

333
00:18:22,212 --> 00:18:23,946
Half a million.

334
00:18:24,079 --> 00:18:26,015
This is how it's gonna work.

335
00:18:26,216 --> 00:18:28,451
I'm gonna take
20% a week.

336
00:18:29,619 --> 00:18:32,788
Hey, we all got bosses,
even I answer to somebody.

337
00:18:32,922 --> 00:18:36,226
But in exchange,
I'll protect you from the gangs.

338
00:18:36,359 --> 00:18:37,660
What gangs?

339
00:18:37,793 --> 00:18:40,230
- And the law.
- This is legal.

340
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:42,432
And if you attacked by locusts,
I'll spray 'em.

341
00:18:42,565 --> 00:18:46,769
Please, don't make me have
to be an asshole about this.

342
00:18:46,902 --> 00:18:49,038
Okay? I protect you.

343
00:18:49,239 --> 00:18:50,573
And you pay me a commission.

344
00:18:50,706 --> 00:18:52,908
[thud]
Capisce?

345
00:19:00,950 --> 00:19:02,452
That's really
all you're gonna take?

346
00:19:02,585 --> 00:19:05,087
What did I just say?
We're partners.

347
00:19:05,255 --> 00:19:08,891
You make the money,
and I make sure you keep it.

348
00:19:09,892 --> 00:19:11,361
Do we have a deal?

349
00:19:11,494 --> 00:19:14,497
- Do I have a choice?
- Absolutely not.

350
00:19:16,466 --> 00:19:19,269
[soft rock]

351
00:19:19,369 --> 00:19:21,904
- [doorbell ringing]
- What happened to my bottle?

352
00:19:22,037 --> 00:19:23,406
- I was thirsty.
- You don't want it.

353
00:19:23,539 --> 00:19:25,475
It's got blood all over it.
Open the door.

354
00:19:26,876 --> 00:19:29,579
When you're not driving a cab,
what kind of car do you drive?

355
00:19:29,712 --> 00:19:31,681
Pssh, the repo man took it.

356
00:19:31,814 --> 00:19:33,483
Here's some money.

357
00:19:34,650 --> 00:19:36,986
I want you
to buy me this car.

358
00:19:39,555 --> 00:19:42,057
- A Navigator?
- Yep, new one, black,

359
00:19:42,191 --> 00:19:44,460
and you drive for me now.

360
00:19:44,594 --> 00:19:46,095
What?

361
00:19:47,597 --> 00:19:49,432
Two grand a week.

362
00:19:51,301 --> 00:19:54,304
My gangster.
[laughing]

363
00:19:55,204 --> 00:19:56,772
Let's go to the hotel.

364
00:19:56,906 --> 00:19:59,174
Stop with that gangster shit.

365
00:20:01,444 --> 00:20:03,346
[rock and roll]

366
00:20:16,091 --> 00:20:17,259
Okay, Tyson,
I need you here

367
00:20:17,393 --> 00:20:19,695
tomorrow morning
at 10:00 AM.

368
00:20:19,829 --> 00:20:22,398
Wear a collared shirt,
10:00 AM.

369
00:21:08,778 --> 00:21:11,414
[distant cars rattling]

370
00:21:28,698 --> 00:21:30,666
[doorbell ringing]

371
00:21:31,901 --> 00:21:33,803
Can I help you, Mister...

372
00:21:33,936 --> 00:21:35,405
Manfredi.

373
00:21:35,405 --> 00:21:37,039
Can you call me a cab?

374
00:21:37,172 --> 00:21:38,841
Oh, we don't really get

375
00:21:38,974 --> 00:21:40,610
a lot of cabs around here,

376
00:21:40,743 --> 00:21:43,112
- but you can call an Uber.
- Oh, yeah, what's the number?

377
00:21:43,245 --> 00:21:45,214
There's no number,
you just use the app

378
00:21:45,415 --> 00:21:48,183
- on your phone.
- Oh.

379
00:21:49,419 --> 00:21:50,586
Do you have an app
on your phone?

380
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:52,254
Of course.

381
00:21:53,456 --> 00:21:55,725
Ms. McNamara,
call me an Uber.

382
00:21:58,293 --> 00:22:01,130
[country music playing]

383
00:22:10,906 --> 00:22:15,511
<i>♪ I been workin' this job
nine to five... ♪</i>

384
00:22:18,147 --> 00:22:22,852
<i>Minimum wage and overtime ♪</i>

385
00:22:23,753 --> 00:22:25,621
<i>But here comes a few days ♪</i>

386
00:22:25,755 --> 00:22:29,224
<i>Of unpaid vacation ♪</i>

387
00:22:30,192 --> 00:22:34,329
<i>♪ And there ain't no way,
José, I'll waste 'em ♪</i>

388
00:22:34,464 --> 00:22:37,366
- Is this seat taken?
- It's all yours.

389
00:22:38,768 --> 00:22:40,369
Good evening.

390
00:22:40,503 --> 00:22:43,172
- How you doing?
- Good.

391
00:22:43,973 --> 00:22:45,274
What'll it be?

392
00:22:45,475 --> 00:22:47,477
Well, I assume
you don't have chianti.

393
00:22:47,577 --> 00:22:49,679
You assume correctly.

394
00:22:49,812 --> 00:22:52,081
- Okay.
- What you need's a bourbon.

395
00:22:52,214 --> 00:22:53,883
Yeah, and why is that?

396
00:22:54,016 --> 00:22:56,185
Well, because I was really
hoping you'd buy me one.

397
00:22:56,318 --> 00:22:57,720
[chuckling]

398
00:22:57,853 --> 00:22:59,288
You'll have to forgive
my friend here,

399
00:22:59,489 --> 00:23:01,524
mister,
he's a goddamn mooch.

400
00:23:01,657 --> 00:23:04,994
Hey, the answer is
always no until you ask.

401
00:23:05,127 --> 00:23:07,630
I'll have a bourbon for me
and my two pals here.

402
00:23:07,763 --> 00:23:10,566
- See?
- Bourbon it is.

403
00:23:11,734 --> 00:23:13,636
Is it all right to eat here?

404
00:23:14,770 --> 00:23:16,772
Best seat
in the house.

405
00:23:16,906 --> 00:23:18,240
And what do you suggest?

406
00:23:18,373 --> 00:23:20,109
You find better ribs
in Tulsa--

407
00:23:20,242 --> 00:23:21,811
[raps counter]
- you let me know.

408
00:23:21,944 --> 00:23:23,946
Ah, then ribs it is.

409
00:23:27,983 --> 00:23:29,519
So, where's home, friend?

410
00:23:29,652 --> 00:23:31,621
I'm gonna give you
two guesses,

411
00:23:31,754 --> 00:23:33,823
but I bet
you'll get it in one.

412
00:23:34,657 --> 00:23:38,293
- New York.
- You're good, very good.

413
00:23:38,427 --> 00:23:40,295
I couldn't help notice,
are those

414
00:23:40,429 --> 00:23:41,997
lizard boots
you're wearing?

415
00:23:42,131 --> 00:23:44,600
Yes, sir, they are.

416
00:23:44,734 --> 00:23:47,002
Made in Texas
just like me.

417
00:23:47,136 --> 00:23:50,205
Check these out.

418
00:23:50,339 --> 00:23:52,141
Made in Italy,
like my old man.

419
00:23:52,274 --> 00:23:55,811
Well, how about that?
We both like dinosaurs.

420
00:23:55,945 --> 00:23:57,613
There you go.

421
00:23:57,747 --> 00:24:00,115
<i>Like a beer can ♪</i>

422
00:24:00,249 --> 00:24:01,917
- Salud.
- Salud.

423
00:24:03,919 --> 00:24:06,055
<i>Like a beer can ♪</i>

424
00:24:07,923 --> 00:24:10,259
<i>No, nothing picks me up ♪</i>

425
00:24:10,392 --> 00:24:12,562
<i>Like a beer can ♪</i>

426
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:19,702
I'm no expert,
but I'm pretty sure

427
00:24:19,835 --> 00:24:21,571
that's not
a Lincoln Navigator.

428
00:24:21,571 --> 00:24:23,205
It's my mom's.

429
00:24:23,338 --> 00:24:24,774
And?

430
00:24:24,907 --> 00:24:27,176
Had to go home and get it
after the car dealership.

431
00:24:27,309 --> 00:24:30,613
- Where's the Navigator?
- He wouldn't sell me one.

432
00:24:30,746 --> 00:24:32,915
- You show him the cash?
- What happened was

433
00:24:33,048 --> 00:24:35,685
he called me a crack dealer,
threatened to call the police.

434
00:24:42,457 --> 00:24:44,860
Take me there.

435
00:24:44,994 --> 00:24:47,597
[music]

436
00:25:00,075 --> 00:25:02,778
Good morning.
How can I help you?

437
00:25:06,148 --> 00:25:08,317
[soft chatter]

438
00:25:08,450 --> 00:25:11,887
No one's gonna know,
what are you worried about?

439
00:25:13,723 --> 00:25:15,390
Uh-huh.

440
00:25:15,524 --> 00:25:18,828
Listen, uh,
let me call you back.

441
00:25:20,329 --> 00:25:22,732
Donnie Shore.
What can I do you for?

442
00:25:22,865 --> 00:25:24,734
Perry Cuomo,
nice to meet you.

443
00:25:24,867 --> 00:25:27,737
It seems we have
a slight misunderstanding.

444
00:25:27,870 --> 00:25:29,939
See, my associate
was in earlier,

445
00:25:30,072 --> 00:25:33,475
trying to buy that Navigator
that you got downstairs,

446
00:25:33,643 --> 00:25:35,410
but you wouldn't
sell it to him.

447
00:25:35,544 --> 00:25:37,546
Oh, boy, I am so sorry.

448
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:39,181
Why, Donnie?

449
00:25:39,314 --> 00:25:41,651
Well, you know, it was
a total misunderstanding.

450
00:25:41,751 --> 00:25:43,452
Like you said yourself.

451
00:25:43,653 --> 00:25:45,855
The truth is,
he's a good kid.

452
00:25:45,988 --> 00:25:48,791
Probably never had
a day of trouble in his life.

453
00:25:48,924 --> 00:25:51,927
You see the problem is,
you see a young Black guy

454
00:25:52,061 --> 00:25:53,996
with a mountain of money--
right away, you say,

455
00:25:54,129 --> 00:25:55,731
hey, he's gotta be
a drug dealer.

456
00:25:55,865 --> 00:25:57,667
- Oh.
- But I walk in,

457
00:25:57,667 --> 00:25:59,534
in a nice suit...

458
00:25:59,669 --> 00:26:01,837
and you're
not afraid anymore.

459
00:26:01,971 --> 00:26:04,139
You see,
the irony is...

460
00:26:05,140 --> 00:26:06,976
he's afraid
of the wrong thing.

461
00:26:08,110 --> 00:26:11,714
- I'm not following.
- Well, follow this.

462
00:26:13,683 --> 00:26:15,685
Aah-- I'm calling the police.

463
00:26:15,818 --> 00:26:17,820
Hey, let me get
the phone for ya.

464
00:26:20,055 --> 00:26:21,824
Here's the deal, Donnie.

465
00:26:21,957 --> 00:26:24,259
You're gonna sell
my friend over here

466
00:26:24,393 --> 00:26:25,828
the black Navigator

467
00:26:25,961 --> 00:26:28,430
for $50,000 cash.

468
00:26:28,563 --> 00:26:30,833
- Loaded.
- Loaded.

469
00:26:31,767 --> 00:26:34,704
- Deal?
- Okay.

470
00:26:35,871 --> 00:26:37,707
This wasn't necessary.

471
00:26:37,807 --> 00:26:41,143
[funk music]

472
00:26:48,718 --> 00:26:50,552
This is crazy.

473
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:52,855
I forgot how good
ice cream is.

474
00:26:52,988 --> 00:26:54,924
They didn't give you
ice cream in jail?

475
00:26:55,057 --> 00:26:56,625
No.

476
00:26:56,759 --> 00:26:59,729
Usually it was tiramisu.

477
00:27:00,796 --> 00:27:02,397
That's a joke, right?

478
00:27:05,835 --> 00:27:08,103
Eh...
[gasping]

479
00:27:08,237 --> 00:27:09,638
Enough.

480
00:27:09,772 --> 00:27:12,441
I'm gonna go wash up,
I'll meet you back at the car,

481
00:27:12,574 --> 00:27:14,810
we're gonna go see Bodhi.

482
00:27:35,464 --> 00:27:37,833
Hey.

483
00:27:39,935 --> 00:27:41,636
How you doin', Fred?

484
00:27:41,771 --> 00:27:44,106
- I've been better.
- Try the Advil.

485
00:27:44,239 --> 00:27:45,775
Thanks.

486
00:27:47,142 --> 00:27:48,911
What's with this puss?

487
00:27:49,044 --> 00:27:51,113
That's how you
welcome customers?

488
00:27:51,246 --> 00:27:53,182
Are you a customer now?

489
00:27:54,549 --> 00:27:56,952
You know, you're
in the service business.

490
00:27:57,086 --> 00:27:59,021
You gotta be welcoming.

491
00:28:01,190 --> 00:28:04,259
- This is Tyson, by the way.
- What's up?

492
00:28:05,627 --> 00:28:06,695
I got something for you.

493
00:28:06,829 --> 00:28:08,630
Security camera.

494
00:28:10,165 --> 00:28:11,901
And before you say
anything, yes,

495
00:28:12,034 --> 00:28:14,136
I get the irony.

496
00:28:18,808 --> 00:28:20,910
So, how much did
we make today?

497
00:28:21,043 --> 00:28:23,813
Um, <i>we</i> made

498
00:28:23,813 --> 00:28:26,181
a little
over five grand so far.

499
00:28:26,315 --> 00:28:29,051
You're a sarcastic
little prick, aren't you?

500
00:28:30,719 --> 00:28:33,288
So, tell me, where do
you get your weed from?

501
00:28:33,422 --> 00:28:35,290
There's a greenhouse
and a 40-acre farm

502
00:28:35,424 --> 00:28:37,092
a couple hours north of here.

503
00:28:37,226 --> 00:28:39,829
That's where I buy.
They're licensed.

504
00:28:39,929 --> 00:28:42,297
- Who are "they"?
- A guy named Jimmy.

505
00:28:42,431 --> 00:28:44,834
Is he a front for somebody?
'Cause a lot of these farms

506
00:28:44,967 --> 00:28:47,870
are fronts for cartels,
you gotta know your risks.

507
00:28:48,003 --> 00:28:50,639
